  "method_choice_rationale": "When candidate PCA and SVD methods produce equivalent subspaces on centered data, the tie is broken deterministically by method_priority ('sklearn_pca' first). sklearn PCA performs internal sample-mean centering during transformation and exposes a production-standard estimator interface, eliminating train-serving skew. Solver scaling note: from_scratch_covariance relies on sequential power iteration with Hotelling deflation (A <- A - lambda * v @ v.T). Extracting k components requires k sequential convergence loops over the d x d covariance matrix (O(k * max_iter * d^2)), causing runtime to scale linearly/superlinearly with rank k, whereas SVD solves all components jointly.",
